WEBVTT

1
00:02:06.576 --> 00:02:07.770
Bobby.

2
00:02:08.678 --> 00:02:09.872
Bobby.

3
00:02:10.714 --> 00:02:11.942
No!

4
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.924
All right. we lined up?

5
00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:41.297
Get that line.

6
00:03:48.979 --> 00:03:51.709
Put the stern line on quick.

7
00:04:13.837 --> 00:04:15.270
Bobby!

8
00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:21.133
Hey. baby!

9
00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.080
Missed you.

10
00:04:36.593 --> 00:04:38.788
Hey. big man. how you doing?

11
00:04:45.869 --> 00:04:48.235
- Hey. Murph!
- Hey. Ethel.

12
00:04:48.538 --> 00:04:50.335
How you doing? Welcome home.

13
00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.735
- You seen Deb and my boy?
- No. I'm sorry.

14
00:04:52.943 --> 00:04:53.967
Ma!

15
00:04:56.212 --> 00:04:58.646
- How you doing. beautiful?
- Hello. Bobby.

16
00:05:00.817 --> 00:05:02.307
Home safe.

17
00:05:09.826 --> 00:05:10.952
Who's that?

18
00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:14.553
- OI' Ben.
- No.

19
00:05:15.532 --> 00:05:16.999
Poor old guy.

20
00:05:18.301 --> 00:05:19.495
Hey. Linda.

21
00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.463
- Hey. boss.
- What's the score?

22
00:05:25.709 --> 00:05:26.937
My kind of numbers.

23
00:05:27.143 --> 00:05:29.509
I lost Ben Pulley.
He passed away onboard.

24
00:05:31.982 --> 00:05:33.609
Sorry to hear that.

25
00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.474
How'd you hit it. Billy?

26
00:05:38.188 --> 00:05:39.883
Didn't hit very hard. did you?

27
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:43.082
We all have slumps. but you're overdue
to break out of yours.

28
00:05:43.293 --> 00:05:45.761
Did you hear the lady?
Ben Pulley's dead.

29
00:05:45.962 --> 00:05:50.365
That old man pickled himself to death
drinking 7& 7s chasing Narragansetts.

30
00:05:50.567 --> 00:05:54.799
Linda. with Ben. it was never
a question of "if." but "when."

31
00:05:55.438 --> 00:05:57.338
- I'll bury him.
- I'll pay for it.

32
00:05:57.741 --> 00:05:59.231
See. you got what you wanted.

33
00:05:59.776 --> 00:06:02.973
Bring in your fish.
It shouldn't take too long.

34
00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:28.558
8-5.

35
00:07:34.838 --> 00:07:36.203
4-7-5.

36
00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.718
Murph.

37
00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.320
Sign my ledger.

38
00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:05.462
Shatford.

39
00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:08.994
Sign my ledger.

40
00:08:13.443 --> 00:08:14.432
What's the matter?

41
00:08:14.644 --> 00:08:16.509
It's $2221.
Aren't we a little short?

42
00:08:19.549 --> 00:08:22.382
We were sharing up last night.
I thought it'd be three plus.

43
00:08:25.288 --> 00:08:30.021
You stocked 21.000 pounds at 3.50
a pound. That comes to $ 73.000.

44
00:08:30.293 --> 00:08:34.889
Minus $35.000 for bait. tackle. fuel.
That comes out to $38.500.

45
00:08:35.198 --> 00:08:36.722
I get half. I own the boat.

46
00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:39.766
Your captain takes double share.
four crewmen get a share each.

47
00:08:39.969 --> 00:08:42.597
And a rookie like you.
three-quarters share.

48
00:08:42.806 --> 00:08:45.866
That comes to $2221.

49
00:08:46.509 --> 00:08:47.908
What it is. is what it is.

50
00:08:48.378 --> 00:08:49.777
Sign the ledger.

51
00:08:56.519 --> 00:08:57.679
Moran.

52
00:09:01.991 --> 00:09:04.221
You going out again this season.
skipper?

53
00:09:04.427 --> 00:09:05.587
Why?

54
00:09:07.063 --> 00:09:08.428
You got a site in Florida?

55
00:09:11.034 --> 00:09:12.467
Bradenton Beach.

56
00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.935
<i>The Cecile.</i>

57
00:09:16.372 --> 00:09:18.272
Pack your shit and get out.

58
00:09:19.909 --> 00:09:21.376
You like Florida?

59
00:09:22.545 --> 00:09:25.070
Well. it beats the Grand Banks
in October.

60
00:09:25.748 --> 00:09:29.013
It gets rough up here.
Dougie likes the sun down there.

61
00:09:29.953 --> 00:09:32.148
Or he thinks he'll score better
with another captain.

62
00:09:32.522 --> 00:09:33.580
I didn't say that.

63
00:09:34.224 --> 00:09:35.589
Yes. you did.

64
00:09:37.393 --> 00:09:38.382
Goodbye.

65
00:09:39.596 --> 00:09:44.431
Here's your cut. $5923.76.
Sign the ledger.

66
00:09:45.602 --> 00:09:47.729
That's a record low for you.
isn't it?

67
00:09:48.204 --> 00:09:51.401
Next time. track Linda.
She'll take you where the fish are.

68
00:09:52.408 --> 00:09:54.569
You're getting to be rude. you know?

69
00:09:54.911 --> 00:09:57.402
I like you. Billy.
I always have.

70
00:09:57.614 --> 00:09:59.081
But I like my boat better.

71
00:09:59.282 --> 00:10:02.342
If you can't make it pay.
I'll find somebody who can.

72
00:10:02.852 --> 00:10:04.683
You trying to put a charge up my ass?

73
00:10:05.688 --> 00:10:07.485
You're on a cold streak.

74
00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.590
I'm encouraging you
to catch fish.

75
00:10:09.792 --> 00:10:12.226
I'll bring you more fish
than you ever dreamed of.

76
00:10:12.428 --> 00:10:15.124
Next time I fish the Grand Banks.
they won't be so grand.

77
00:10:15.331 --> 00:10:17.299
You just struck out
on the Grand Banks.

78
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.592
Then I'll go further.

79
00:10:20.904 --> 00:10:23.464
Don't even think about it.
I want my boat back.

80
00:10:23.673 --> 00:10:25.573
And I want to catch some fish.

81
00:10:25.775 --> 00:10:26.764
It's what I do.

82
00:10:27.477 --> 00:10:28.466
Not lately.

83
00:10:28.678 --> 00:10:31.044
Want to yank my site. you go ahead.

84
00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.234
- Murph.
- Hey. skip.

85
00:10:55.405 --> 00:10:58.203
What are you doing out here?
Get in there. Get drunk.

86
00:10:58.875 --> 00:11:00.570
Waiting on my ex...

87
00:11:01.144 --> 00:11:02.475
...and my son.

88
00:11:06.983 --> 00:11:09.577
Give him lots of
hugs and kisses tonight.

89
00:11:10.486 --> 00:11:13.250
You don't gotta remind me
to do that. skip.

90
00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.324
Ladies. you're looking fine.
How you doing?

91
00:11:19.529 --> 00:11:22.020
Can I buy you a drink?
What. what. what?

92
00:11:28.871 --> 00:11:30.338
Hey. rookie.

93
00:11:32.408 --> 00:11:34.035
What are you so happy about?

94
00:11:35.178 --> 00:11:38.306
It wasn't exactly a slammer
up on the Grand Banks.

95
00:11:38.514 --> 00:11:40.106
Isn't it past your bedtime?

96
00:11:42.018 --> 00:11:43.747
Bugs. how you making out?

97
00:11:43.953 --> 00:11:45.352
I'm not.

98
00:11:47.557 --> 00:11:49.991
I don't know.
Maybe I smell like fish.

99
00:11:50.193 --> 00:11:53.492
- You need a new deodorant.
- Maybe I need a new face.

100
00:11:56.599 --> 00:11:58.897
Frickin' Alfred Pierre.

101
00:12:00.103 --> 00:12:04.062
They were upstairs. they come down.
a little refreshment.

102
00:12:04.273 --> 00:12:06.173
Now they're going back up again.

103
00:12:06.376 --> 00:12:09.038
Half an hour ago. they shook
the lamps over the bar.

104
00:12:09.245 --> 00:12:12.976
Last time she brought her sister.
You should've seen the lamps then.

105
00:12:14.951 --> 00:12:16.816
How do he do it. mon?

106
00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.818
I think he's fishin'
with a longer pole. Bugs.

107
00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:31.958
What happened?

108
00:12:32.168 --> 00:12:36.298
They had a sale on kids' shoes
at Ames.

109
00:12:36.506 --> 00:12:37.700
Sorry.

110
00:12:39.075 --> 00:12:40.474
No problem.

111
00:12:41.411 --> 00:12:42.241
Hi.

112
00:12:42.945 --> 00:12:44.207
Hello.

113
00:12:47.083 --> 00:12:48.812
So you want to have a drink?

114
00:12:51.587 --> 00:12:52.679
Come on. Debra.

115
00:12:52.889 --> 00:12:54.880
What do you say. for old times' sake?

116
00:12:55.091 --> 00:12:57.252
It was the old times that killed us.

117
00:12:59.962 --> 00:13:01.259
Is that what it was?

118
00:13:04.867 --> 00:13:06.129
There you go.

119
00:13:06.903 --> 00:13:09.371
I'm a little short.
It wasn't exactly a slammer.

120
00:13:10.339 --> 00:13:11.328
Half for you.

121
00:13:13.443 --> 00:13:14.432
You sure?

122
00:13:14.644 --> 00:13:15.770
Yeah. I'm working.

123
00:13:21.551 --> 00:13:22.916
Want to come with your daddy?

124
00:13:24.921 --> 00:13:26.320
Shoot some pool?

125
00:13:28.724 --> 00:13:30.191
Have a drink?

126
00:13:36.099 --> 00:13:38.158
Just bring him home in an hour.

127
00:13:57.587 --> 00:13:59.350
Good shot. buddy.

128
00:13:59.655 --> 00:14:02.283
All right. Sully. you think about it.

129
00:14:02.492 --> 00:14:03.584
All right?

130
00:14:06.963 --> 00:14:08.555
Bugs.

131
00:14:10.733 --> 00:14:11.995
Murph. come here.

132
00:14:12.201 --> 00:14:15.102
Here comes your fearless leader.
Captain Billy Tyne.

133
00:14:15.304 --> 00:14:18.102
I got a feeling skipper's
coming to give us bad news.

134
00:14:19.709 --> 00:14:22.109
Lady's not only pretty. she's smart.

135
00:14:24.147 --> 00:14:25.842
Yeah. we're going back out.

136
00:14:26.549 --> 00:14:27.948
What'd I tell you?

137
00:14:29.685 --> 00:14:31.710
- When?
- A few days.

138
00:14:31.921 --> 00:14:33.115
"Few" means two?

139
00:14:33.689 --> 00:14:34.713
Two days is right.

140
00:14:34.924 --> 00:14:36.585
Skip. we just got back in.

141
00:14:36.792 --> 00:14:39.420
You don't want your site.
a replacement's a call away.

142
00:14:42.565 --> 00:14:44.863
Join me. don't join me.

143
00:14:45.268 --> 00:14:47.998
<i>There's time for one last shot.
The Andrea Gail will take it.</i>

144
00:14:48.204 --> 00:14:51.765
This time I promise you. we'll
come back with a shitload of fish.

145
00:14:52.208 --> 00:14:53.903
Excuse me. men. madam.

146
00:14:59.849 --> 00:15:01.180
What are you gonna do?

147
00:15:01.684 --> 00:15:04.676
I'm gonna tell him to
stick his head up his ass.

148
00:15:04.921 --> 00:15:06.252
I'd like to hear that.

149
00:15:07.223 --> 00:15:08.247
Hear what?

150
00:15:08.457 --> 00:15:11.017
I'd like to hear you tell him
to stick it up his ass.

151
00:15:11.227 --> 00:15:12.489
Go on. Bob.

152
00:15:17.233 --> 00:15:20.964
Yeah. that's just how I'll tell him
as soon as we get back.

153
00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:22.728
You're a bastard.

154
00:15:23.372 --> 00:15:25.602
Why? Why do I even love you?

155
00:15:25.808 --> 00:15:27.571
- Come on.
- No. Why? Why. Bobby?

156
00:15:28.077 --> 00:15:31.012
When you get the answer. tell me.
I could use it myself.

157
00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:34.176
- Get laid. Bugsy.
- Easy for you to say.

158
00:15:43.492 --> 00:15:44.789
Go on up there.

159
00:15:44.994 --> 00:15:46.791
Don't make the same mistake I did.

160
00:15:56.973 --> 00:15:58.964
You're going away again?

161
00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.641
Yeah.

162
00:16:03.246 --> 00:16:05.271
Take me with you.

163
00:16:09.252 --> 00:16:10.514
Come here.

164
00:16:13.889 --> 00:16:14.878
Go back. Bobby.

165
00:16:15.958 --> 00:16:18.449
Go back to what you did before.

166
00:16:18.661 --> 00:16:21.687
- Pack cod. repair tackle.
- I'm sick of that.

167
00:16:22.164 --> 00:16:23.688
It's safe and it pays.

168
00:16:24.567 --> 00:16:25.932
Not enough.

169
00:16:26.569 --> 00:16:28.628
Just one more time. I promise.

170
00:16:28.904 --> 00:16:31.600
I have to try it again.
We need the money. baby.

171
00:16:31.807 --> 00:16:34.401
Money. It's always about the money.

172
00:16:35.278 --> 00:16:39.408
Well. I got a divorce lawyer.
a mountain of debt.

173
00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:44.351
And there's your two kids.
You gotta get them back.

174
00:16:46.689 --> 00:16:48.486
Do you think you'll love them?

175
00:16:48.858 --> 00:16:50.587
They're yours. aren't they?

176
00:17:10.446 --> 00:17:11.936
Hey. beautiful.

177
00:17:12.248 --> 00:17:13.374
Yeah. you.

178
00:17:14.517 --> 00:17:16.041
Buy you a drink?

179
00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:19.914
Seeing as I got two in front of me.
I don't think so.

180
00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:22.815
I'm not very observant. am I?

181
00:17:24.126 --> 00:17:27.425
I got a feeling. yeah.
along with a lot of other things.

182
00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:29.393
Why don't we start over?

183
00:17:30.633 --> 00:17:33.761
You know what would look good on you?
Me.

184
00:17:36.872 --> 00:17:38.134
No good?

185
00:17:42.144 --> 00:17:44.510
Have a drink. It's not that bad.

186
00:17:47.049 --> 00:17:49.040
Thank you. Here's to crime.

187
00:17:55.558 --> 00:17:57.150
You're pathetic.

188
00:18:00.463 --> 00:18:02.226
You still want to be a fisherman?

189
00:18:02.431 --> 00:18:05.025
Who told you I wanted to be
a fisherman?

190
00:18:05.401 --> 00:18:06.800
You want to come with me.

191
00:18:07.002 --> 00:18:10.438
I want to come with you.
but I don't want to be a fisherman.

192
00:18:15.311 --> 00:18:16.903
You know. buddy...

193
00:18:19.215 --> 00:18:22.810
...one of these days your mom's
gonna find you a new dad.

194
00:18:23.018 --> 00:18:25.248
I don't want a new dad.

195
00:18:25.454 --> 00:18:26.614
I'm sorry.

196
00:18:26.822 --> 00:18:29.586
Your mom can't sit around
by herself all the time.

197
00:18:30.192 --> 00:18:32.126
She isn't sitting around.

198
00:18:49.378 --> 00:18:51.369
I'm sure he's a good guy.

199
00:18:52.481 --> 00:18:55.917
I know your mom wouldn't take up
with anybody but a good guy.

200
00:18:59.789 --> 00:19:01.347
And you know. buddy...

201
00:19:02.057 --> 00:19:05.288
...the most important thing is
that you and Mommy are happy.

202
00:19:06.662 --> 00:19:09.756
Can we talk about something else now?

203
00:19:21.277 --> 00:19:23.404
I miss you too. buddy.

204
00:19:29.618 --> 00:19:31.984
I miss you so damn much.

205
00:19:33.722 --> 00:19:36.486
What'd you say your name was again?

206
00:19:37.059 --> 00:19:39.084
Irene. Is that so tough?

207
00:19:39.295 --> 00:19:40.990
I'm sorry. Listen.

208
00:19:42.431 --> 00:19:44.490
Could I maybe take you home?

209
00:19:45.501 --> 00:19:46.490
I don't think so.

210
00:19:47.636 --> 00:19:51.834
I came to watch the game. Instead I
got schnockered with Bugsy.

211
00:19:53.576 --> 00:19:56.340
- What does Bugsy stand for anyway?
- Michael.

212
00:19:56.946 --> 00:19:59.346
That's a nice name.
Why don't you use it?

213
00:19:59.782 --> 00:20:01.443
Because people know me as Bugsy.

214
00:20:04.019 --> 00:20:06.510
I'm gonna shove off now.
Big day tomorrow.

215
00:20:06.722 --> 00:20:09.247
I can't take you home?

216
00:20:09.458 --> 00:20:11.153
What. in a wheelbarrow?

217
00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.260
Crew guys like you never have cars.

218
00:20:13.462 --> 00:20:16.090
Lay off. I got feelings too.

219
00:20:16.298 --> 00:20:19.233
Where. down in your pants?

220
00:20:20.536 --> 00:20:23.699
Jesus. lady. where's the passion
in your life?

221
00:20:23.906 --> 00:20:25.931
Home in bed.

222
00:20:26.208 --> 00:20:28.574
One of them's 6. the other one's 8.

223
00:20:30.246 --> 00:20:33.409
All I can say is.
there's some lucky kids.

224
00:20:34.216 --> 00:20:35.581
They got a wonderful mother.

225
00:20:41.323 --> 00:20:43.416
You're not messing with me. are you?

226
00:20:45.561 --> 00:20:47.893
Haven't got time.
We're going out in two days.

227
00:20:49.565 --> 00:20:51.897
Well. I'm sorry to hear that. Michael.

228
00:20:53.435 --> 00:20:54.800
Gotta go.

229
00:20:56.505 --> 00:20:57.870
What do you mean?

230
00:21:00.075 --> 00:21:01.736
- Where you going?
- Have these.

231
00:21:01.944 --> 00:21:03.605
- Thank you.
- See you.

232
00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:09.643
- Bye. Ethel.
- See you.

233
00:21:27.736 --> 00:21:28.760
Watch your step.

234
00:21:38.847 --> 00:21:40.678
I smell Coppertone.

235
00:21:40.883 --> 00:21:42.851
That means that
Captain Linda Greenlaw...

236
00:21:43.052 --> 00:21:46.317
...a lady vain about her nose.
is in my wheelhouse.

237
00:21:46.522 --> 00:21:47.887
Make that Hawaiian Tropic.

238
00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:50.183
At least I got the nose right.

239
00:21:51.327 --> 00:21:53.989
Your guys are loading bait
and groceries.

240
00:21:55.130 --> 00:21:58.099
- You doing a turnaround?
- No rest for the weary.

241
00:21:58.300 --> 00:22:00.530
There you go.
Flaunting your work ethic.

242
00:22:00.869 --> 00:22:03.030
I don't have a work ethic.
I just have work.

243
00:22:03.238 --> 00:22:05.138
If I'm gonna catch up to you.

244
00:22:06.208 --> 00:22:07.971
I love to watch you study charts.

245
00:22:08.177 --> 00:22:09.474
Why?

246
00:22:09.945 --> 00:22:11.412
You know them all by heart.

247
00:22:12.481 --> 00:22:15.314
What's special about today
that you're blowing smoke up my ass?

248
00:22:15.517 --> 00:22:16.848
I thought I'd make a pass.

249
00:22:20.756 --> 00:22:24.419
You see. I'm looking for a guy
to come home to Maine with me...

250
00:22:24.627 --> 00:22:26.094
...buy a house and raise kids.

251
00:22:26.295 --> 00:22:28.229
What does that guy and you do after?

252
00:22:29.732 --> 00:22:32.997
The thing is. I'm happy.
I'm happy I'm fit to do this.

253
00:22:33.202 --> 00:22:35.329
I just don't see the romance in it.

254
00:22:35.571 --> 00:22:38.438
But you've got it. Captain Greenlaw.

255
00:22:38.907 --> 00:22:40.602
You do. Believe me.

256
00:22:40.809 --> 00:22:42.572
I've seen them come and go.

257
00:22:42.778 --> 00:22:46.270
The day I laid eyes on you. I said.
"She's gonna be a good one."

258
00:22:46.915 --> 00:22:48.815
You can't be good unless you love it.

259
00:22:51.353 --> 00:22:53.150
The fog's just lifting.

260
00:22:54.523 --> 00:22:57.048
You throw off your bow line.
throw off your stern.

261
00:22:58.627 --> 00:23:00.527
You head out the South Channel...

262
00:23:00.729 --> 00:23:03.960
...past Rocky Neck.
Ten Pound Island...

263
00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:08.097
...past Niles Pond.
where I skated as a kid.

264
00:23:08.904 --> 00:23:10.064
Blow your horn...

265
00:23:10.272 --> 00:23:13.332
...and wave to the lighthouse
keeper's kid on Thatcher Island.

266
00:23:14.276 --> 00:23:15.834
Then the birds show up.

267
00:23:16.045 --> 00:23:17.603
Black-backs...

268
00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:20.747
...herring gulls. big dump ducks.

269
00:23:22.584 --> 00:23:24.074
The sun hits you.

270
00:23:24.286 --> 00:23:26.982
Head north. open up to 12.

271
00:23:28.057 --> 00:23:29.115
You're steaming now.

272
00:23:29.992 --> 00:23:32.961
The guys are busy.
you're in charge.

273
00:23:34.263 --> 00:23:37.494
You know what?
You're a goddamn swordboat captain.

274
00:23:40.703 --> 00:23:42.898
Is there anything better in the world?

275
00:23:56.251 --> 00:23:57.343
Sully.

276
00:24:00.589 --> 00:24:02.420
So what do you think?

277
00:24:06.762 --> 00:24:07.888
You been busy?

278
00:24:08.097 --> 00:24:09.496
Busy enough.

279
00:24:09.698 --> 00:24:12.360
I was working menhaden in Annisquam.

280
00:24:12.701 --> 00:24:14.692
But they laid off Labor Day.

281
00:24:15.337 --> 00:24:16.964
Mended nets over in Fairhaven.

282
00:24:17.172 --> 00:24:19.970
That's crap.
What's this you're doing now?

283
00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:22.741
Helping out a friend.

284
00:24:22.945 --> 00:24:24.412
He paying you?

285
00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.572
He's my friend.

286
00:24:30.986 --> 00:24:32.510
Murphy keep his site?

287
00:24:36.325 --> 00:24:38.020
You want this job or not?

288
00:24:39.928 --> 00:24:41.156
I do.

289
00:25:46.795 --> 00:25:49.730
Lord. did I do that?

290
00:25:52.267 --> 00:25:53.632
Yeah. you did.

291
00:25:54.736 --> 00:25:58.604
But I'm not completely blind.
I can still see out of the other one.

292
00:25:59.808 --> 00:26:01.105
Next time I should break a leg.

293
00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:03.972
Then you can stay home
and collect disability.

294
00:26:04.413 --> 00:26:07.211
Think of all those
handicapped parking spaces.

295
00:26:10.586 --> 00:26:12.781
Tell me last night was worth it.

296
00:26:13.455 --> 00:26:15.218
I can't remember.

297
00:26:15.891 --> 00:26:18.416
Can't remember. my ass.

298
00:26:18.694 --> 00:26:20.992
No. I remember your ass.

299
00:26:23.232 --> 00:26:25.097
Last night was worth it.

300
00:26:26.101 --> 00:26:27.659
There's nothing like
sleeping with you.

301
00:26:29.471 --> 00:26:30.904
Just sleeping...

302
00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:33.037
...lying next to you...

303
00:26:33.976 --> 00:26:35.807
...all warm and sweet.

304
00:26:36.578 --> 00:26:39.206
And me wishing the morning
would never come.

305
00:26:49.191 --> 00:26:50.749
Catching up.

306
00:26:55.864 --> 00:26:59.095
Oh. boy. oh. boy.
Look at that shiner.

307
00:26:59.301 --> 00:27:00.768
Come on. Murph. will you?

308
00:27:02.304 --> 00:27:04.397
Good morning.
Where'd you get the mouse?

309
00:27:04.606 --> 00:27:06.506
Chris "Boom-Boom" Cotter.

310
00:27:09.177 --> 00:27:12.112
Put some hair around that hole.
I bet you could hit it.

311
00:27:13.148 --> 00:27:16.879
Not with a pool cue.
or any other pointed instrument.

312
00:27:19.321 --> 00:27:23.189
What do you know except to cut squid
and take them to bed with you?

313
00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:28.156
Ethel. where you getting
your customers these days?

314
00:27:28.363 --> 00:27:29.955
The welfare office?

315
00:27:30.666 --> 00:27:32.896
Who gave you that scar. tough guy?

316
00:27:33.835 --> 00:27:35.666
Back off! Back off.

317
00:27:35.871 --> 00:27:36.997
Come on. swing it.

318
00:27:37.372 --> 00:27:38.805
You assholes!

319
00:27:41.076 --> 00:27:45.342
How you gonna act onboard if you're
already at each other's throats?

320
00:27:45.547 --> 00:27:46.605
All right. Ma.

321
00:27:48.784 --> 00:27:50.342
See you onboard.

322
00:27:55.157 --> 00:27:58.217
- Alfred Pierre. one for the road?
- No. tanks. Mom.

323
00:27:58.727 --> 00:28:02.026
"No. tanks. Mom."
Guy can't even speak good English.

324
00:28:02.230 --> 00:28:04.357
Well. anyway. can I get you anything?

325
00:28:04.566 --> 00:28:05.897
Let's go. boys.

326
00:28:07.836 --> 00:28:10.134
I'll wait for you in the car. Bobby.

327
00:28:11.840 --> 00:28:14.968
Catch fish. boys. Lots of them.
Full ahead.

328
00:28:15.177 --> 00:28:17.236
Hold down the fort. Quentin.

329
00:28:17.479 --> 00:28:18.810
Thanks. Q.

330
00:28:19.381 --> 00:28:20.507
Thanks. Ethel.

331
00:28:24.453 --> 00:28:25.920
Gotta go. Mom.

332
00:28:28.423 --> 00:28:30.186
The Grand Banks.

333
00:28:30.859 --> 00:28:32.087
I know.

334
00:28:32.294 --> 00:28:35.593
Grand Banks are no joke in October.
All right?

335
00:28:38.934 --> 00:28:40.265
Be careful.

336
00:29:19.141 --> 00:29:21.336
At least we'll get cancer together.

337
00:29:26.882 --> 00:29:29.043
I can't put it off any longer.

338
00:29:29.918 --> 00:29:31.977
I'm not too big on goodbyes.

339
00:29:34.656 --> 00:29:38.387
Don't go. Bobby. I got a bad feeling.

340
00:29:39.861 --> 00:29:41.488
I've been thinking about it.

341
00:29:42.164 --> 00:29:44.530
Then for God's sake. don't go.

342
00:29:44.733 --> 00:29:46.701
I'll moonlight. I'll sell the car.

343
00:29:46.902 --> 00:29:48.927
We'll work nights. weekends.

344
00:29:49.137 --> 00:29:52.595
Whatever it takes. little by little.
we'll put something away.

345
00:29:58.947 --> 00:30:00.380
I gotta go.

346
00:30:09.491 --> 00:30:10.719
Michael.

347
00:30:27.876 --> 00:30:28.706
Irene.

348
00:30:28.910 --> 00:30:30.844
Irene. I knew that.

349
00:30:34.883 --> 00:30:36.851
I just wanted to say goodbye.

350
00:30:38.353 --> 00:30:40.685
No one ever said goodbye to me before.

351
00:30:47.462 --> 00:30:48.724
Well. goodbye. Irene.

352
00:30:49.197 --> 00:30:50.061
Goodbye.

353
00:30:50.265 --> 00:30:52.825
I wish it were night so I could say.
"Good night. Irene."

354
00:30:56.104 --> 00:30:57.435
That'll come later.

355
00:31:01.910 --> 00:31:03.172
Well. you gotta go.

356
00:31:03.979 --> 00:31:05.913
Come on. boys. Let's go.

357
00:31:18.793 --> 00:31:20.192
I love you.

358
00:31:21.062 --> 00:31:23.155
I will always love you. Christina.

359
00:33:03.098 --> 00:33:06.067
Pack it in there good.
We got more coming down.

360
00:33:06.635 --> 00:33:08.626
Did we get all them eggs up there?

361
00:33:20.215 --> 00:33:22.080
<i>We catching some fish</i>

362
00:33:23.551 --> 00:33:25.246
Is that gonna crap out again?

363
00:33:25.453 --> 00:33:26.715
Never!

364
00:34:04.359 --> 00:34:05.621
Do you mind?

365
00:34:09.431 --> 00:34:11.626
Stinks in here. doesn't it?

366
00:34:12.467 --> 00:34:14.094
Not anymore.

367
00:34:26.081 --> 00:34:29.312
<i>Hi. Bobby:
You're somewhere out there...</i>

368
00:34:29.751 --> 00:34:32.720
<i>... on the deep blue. goddamn sea...</i>

369
00:34:33.355 --> 00:34:37.052
<i>... and I'm writing this on a box
of two semi-down pillows...</i>

370
00:34:37.258 --> 00:34:40.022
<i>... that I secretly bought for us
at Penney's.</i>

371
00:34:40.929 --> 00:34:43.124
<i>And I'm smiling to myself because...</i>

372
00:34:43.331 --> 00:34:45.765
<i>... of the surprise I have
in store for you.</i>

373
00:34:46.468 --> 00:34:51.098
<i>I'm talking removal from our dungeon
in the Crow's Nest...</i>

374
00:34:51.940 --> 00:34:54.101
<i>... to our own place.</i>

375
00:34:55.810 --> 00:34:58.040
<i>It's no great shakes...</i>

376
00:34:58.246 --> 00:35:01.272
<i>... but you gotta begin
with a baby shake. right?</i>

377
00:35:03.818 --> 00:35:05.683
<i>Forever love. Bobby.</i>

378
00:35:06.221 --> 00:35:08.519
<i>I'm in this for the long run.</i>

379
00:35:13.361 --> 00:35:16.455
- I'm not intruding. am I?
- You're not intruding.

380
00:35:16.965 --> 00:35:18.523
You're a natural.

381
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:20.934
You've got some old salt
in your blood.

382
00:35:21.136 --> 00:35:22.228
Thanks.

383
00:35:24.806 --> 00:35:27.400
You're a happy man out here.
aren't you?

384
00:35:27.609 --> 00:35:29.042
Today. maybe.

385
00:35:29.811 --> 00:35:31.278
When do you get unhappy?

386
00:35:31.613 --> 00:35:33.137
The day we go home.

387
00:35:33.581 --> 00:35:35.981
Home? I thought the sea
was your home.

388
00:35:38.820 --> 00:35:39.912
You got me there.

389
00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:44.781
But if you were gonna pin me down...

390
00:35:46.294 --> 00:35:49.593
...I guess Pensacola. Florida is home.

391
00:35:49.798 --> 00:35:51.629
My ex lives there. Jodi.

392
00:35:51.833 --> 00:35:53.357
And my kids.

393
00:35:55.670 --> 00:35:59.697
I wasn't very good at doing things
the way they're supposed to be done.

394
00:35:59.908 --> 00:36:01.136
Wife.

395
00:36:02.143 --> 00:36:03.371
Kids.

396
00:36:03.812 --> 00:36:05.746
A house with things in it.
All that stuff.

397
00:36:06.414 --> 00:36:07.881
So why are you so happy?

398
00:36:08.983 --> 00:36:10.951
You just got me on a good day.

399
00:36:11.686 --> 00:36:13.881
I'm doing what I was made to do.

400
00:36:14.656 --> 00:36:17.284
And I got a feeling I'll do it
even better this time.

401
00:36:19.260 --> 00:36:20.420
How about you?

402
00:36:22.363 --> 00:36:25.059
I got a woman I can't stand to be
more than two feet away from.

403
00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:27.129
Congratulations.

404
00:36:28.536 --> 00:36:31.733
Then again. I love to fish.

405
00:36:36.644 --> 00:36:38.441
Son. you've got a problem.

406
00:36:38.947 --> 00:36:40.209
I know.

407
00:36:56.097 --> 00:36:57.291
Here you are.

408
00:37:05.773 --> 00:37:09.573
What do you think? Blue skies.
scattered showers. same old. same old?

409
00:37:09.777 --> 00:37:11.768
- Your guess is as good as mine.
- Or better.

410
00:37:11.980 --> 00:37:13.311
Watch it.

411
00:37:16.518 --> 00:37:18.315
This doesn't look good.

412
00:37:24.626 --> 00:37:26.457
Looks pretty ugly here too.

413
00:37:27.495 --> 00:37:28.587
Pam.

414
00:37:30.064 --> 00:37:33.465
Tell Bernie I need two graphics:
Bermuda and Sable Island.

415
00:37:52.687 --> 00:37:54.018
Good.

416
00:37:55.256 --> 00:37:56.689
What's our course?

417
00:37:56.891 --> 00:38:00.019
I've been sailing 42 years.
Never plotted a course.

418
00:38:01.129 --> 00:38:03.256
I set the compass. I ride it...

419
00:38:03.464 --> 00:38:05.762
...we'll be in Bermuda in no time.

420
00:38:49.143 --> 00:38:50.235
Let's go fishing.

421
00:38:52.146 --> 00:38:54.046
All right. guys. let's hit it!

422
00:38:55.416 --> 00:38:59.750
1000 hooks in the water before dinner.
I want 40 miles out there.

423
00:39:07.161 --> 00:39:09.356
Three-mile buoy out!

424
00:39:09.564 --> 00:39:10.997
Yeah. baby.

425
00:39:19.774 --> 00:39:20.934
Set.

426
00:39:37.058 --> 00:39:38.821
Okay. Sully. put it out.

427
00:39:40.161 --> 00:39:41.856
Highflyer!

428
00:40:08.790 --> 00:40:10.280
Hey. A.P.

429
00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:13.588
May the force be with us.

430
00:40:13.795 --> 00:40:16.355
You want to play with lightsticks.
stick them up your ass.

431
00:40:16.564 --> 00:40:17.394
Easy. Murph.

432
00:40:17.598 --> 00:40:20.431
He's dead weight.
He's been screwing around all night.

433
00:40:20.635 --> 00:40:22.034
A juicer and a head.

434
00:40:22.236 --> 00:40:23.533
Cape Ann. bottom shelf.

435
00:40:23.738 --> 00:40:26.400
Yeah. well. your wife
didn't feel that way.

436
00:40:31.813 --> 00:40:33.678
Hey. knock it off!

437
00:40:33.881 --> 00:40:37.373
I'll head for land and the Newfies
will throw you both in jail!

438
00:40:37.585 --> 00:40:39.109
All right. cap.

439
00:40:39.854 --> 00:40:40.980
Give us some lights.

440
00:40:43.658 --> 00:40:45.023
Come on. Jesus.

441
00:40:45.226 --> 00:40:46.921
Shake. you guys.

442
00:40:47.462 --> 00:40:48.656
Shake!

443
00:40:59.741 --> 00:41:02.175
- Just let it go.
- Your day is coming.

444
00:41:02.376 --> 00:41:05.140
Whenever you're ready.
I'll be right up here.

445
00:41:05.446 --> 00:41:08.176
The job ain't hard enough
without this knucklehead.

446
00:41:35.743 --> 00:41:36.937
Let's go.

447
00:41:42.583 --> 00:41:44.380
We're gonna make some money.

448
00:41:46.187 --> 00:41:47.814
Let's go. boys!

449
00:41:49.924 --> 00:41:51.551
Let's go! Come on!

450
00:42:10.011 --> 00:42:11.205
Come on.

451
00:42:32.200 --> 00:42:33.827
Do it. skip. do it.

452
00:42:34.702 --> 00:42:35.930
Make a killing.

453
00:42:37.705 --> 00:42:38.933
One's on.

454
00:42:39.240 --> 00:42:40.298
Fish on.

455
00:42:44.779 --> 00:42:46.212
Have those gaffs ready.

456
00:42:46.414 --> 00:42:48.814
Don't lose him. Murph.
Don't lose him.

457
00:42:50.885 --> 00:42:52.375
Pull him in. Murph.

458
00:42:58.826 --> 00:43:01.260
All right. now. gaff him. Gaff him!

459
00:43:08.636 --> 00:43:10.228
One. two. three!

460
00:43:26.487 --> 00:43:27.613
Pull him in.

461
00:43:38.766 --> 00:43:40.529
Come on. a little bit more.

462
00:43:46.774 --> 00:43:48.537
So what do you think?

463
00:43:48.809 --> 00:43:50.208
Do you think he'll like it?

464
00:43:50.411 --> 00:43:52.038
He'll love it.

465
00:43:53.581 --> 00:43:55.446
Enough to live with me in it?

466
00:43:56.450 --> 00:43:59.681
By now. honey. you know him
much better than I do.

467
00:44:02.290 --> 00:44:03.689
We're gonna make a go of it.

468
00:44:07.828 --> 00:44:09.625
I got confidence in you.

469
00:44:11.232 --> 00:44:13.166
What. are you putting me on?

470
00:44:16.037 --> 00:44:17.902
He's my precious boy.

471
00:44:18.973 --> 00:44:20.838
And you're the woman for him.

472
00:44:23.411 --> 00:44:25.709
That's something I don't joke about.

473
00:44:29.550 --> 00:44:32.542
<i>The activity down near Bermuda
is deepening rapidly.</i>

474
00:44:32.753 --> 00:44:34.948
<i>Given the warm and volatile
Gulf Stream...</i>

475
00:44:35.156 --> 00:44:39.718
<i>... it won't take much to turn
this tropical storm into a hurricane.</i>

476
00:44:39.927 --> 00:44:42.896
<i>This just in. video of Sable Island.</i>

477
00:45:30.711 --> 00:45:34.738
I put so much ground beef and sausage
in this. it weighed out at 20 pounds.

478
00:45:34.949 --> 00:45:36.814
More than most of our fish weigh.

479
00:45:37.018 --> 00:45:38.883
Skipper say anything about us
coming up short?

480
00:45:39.086 --> 00:45:40.610
He's too scared to say.

481
00:45:40.821 --> 00:45:42.846
Skipper don't get scared.

482
00:45:43.357 --> 00:45:44.551
Just disappointed.

483
00:45:45.726 --> 00:45:47.819
You know why this lasagna weighs
20 pounds?

484
00:45:48.796 --> 00:45:51.026
It tasted like you
threw in a shot put.

485
00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:55.094
I once worked a site
with a guy like you.

486
00:45:55.870 --> 00:45:57.804
The guy had a real bad accident.

487
00:45:59.707 --> 00:46:02.801
Can't even keep track of them
with so many accidents at sea.

488
00:46:04.211 --> 00:46:06.179
Tough to get an ambulance too.

489
00:46:10.551 --> 00:46:11.745
Keep it up.

490
00:46:14.989 --> 00:46:16.684
Highflyer!

491
00:46:21.462 --> 00:46:23.862
A.P.. give me a hand.

492
00:46:25.366 --> 00:46:27.834
Hey. how about a little hand
over here?

493
00:46:28.035 --> 00:46:30.503
You do your job. I'll do mine.

494
00:46:32.373 --> 00:46:33.965
Come on. guys.

495
00:46:35.776 --> 00:46:37.175
Came out here for nothing.

496
00:46:37.378 --> 00:46:39.437
Keep moving. keep moving.

497
00:46:41.715 --> 00:46:44.707
Come on. Sully. let's get
some bait going here.

498
00:47:02.269 --> 00:47:03.668
It's big.

499
00:47:03.871 --> 00:47:05.338
- Something very big.
- Fish on!

500
00:47:05.539 --> 00:47:06.699
Come on. guys.

501
00:47:06.907 --> 00:47:08.067
Oh. yeah.

502
00:47:08.275 --> 00:47:10.140
Come on. Bring it up.

503
00:47:23.924 --> 00:47:24.913
Bring it up.

504
00:47:28.596 --> 00:47:29.722
Get the gaff!

505
00:47:32.733 --> 00:47:34.098
Get it out of here!

506
00:47:34.301 --> 00:47:36.929
Stick him.
Stick it in his head! Good!

507
00:47:44.311 --> 00:47:45.573
Get him off!

508
00:47:46.814 --> 00:47:48.509
- He's got my leg!
- Hang on!

509
00:47:52.453 --> 00:47:55.388
Kick your foot out! Kick it!
Kick your foot out.

510
00:47:55.589 --> 00:47:56.817
Get back!

511
00:48:01.328 --> 00:48:03.626
All right. come on. get it out!

512
00:48:03.864 --> 00:48:04.888
Get it out of here.

513
00:48:05.966 --> 00:48:08.264
- Pull him back!
- Over the side.

514
00:48:09.570 --> 00:48:11.037
You all right?

515
00:48:17.011 --> 00:48:18.979
You're short a boot. rookie!

516
00:48:20.648 --> 00:48:22.445
Beats a leg. don't it?

517
00:48:43.971 --> 00:48:47.805
Okay. we're getting a reading of winds
over 140 knots sustained.

518
00:48:48.008 --> 00:48:50.135
Looks like a category 5.

519
00:49:16.370 --> 00:49:20.101
"Billy Tyne is no fine wine

520
00:49:21.675 --> 00:49:24.303
He's lost his touch with our long line

521
00:49:24.745 --> 00:49:28.306
Steamed here and there and all about

522
00:49:29.350 --> 00:49:31.079
What's our tally?

523
00:49:31.552 --> 00:49:33.110
We've struck out"

524
00:49:39.026 --> 00:49:41.824
All right. okay.
Thank you very much. Thank you.

525
00:49:54.041 --> 00:49:56.601
Why aren't you downstairs
watching the movie?

526
00:49:57.878 --> 00:49:59.607
One of our three movies?

527
00:50:00.314 --> 00:50:01.941
I know them all by heart.

528
00:50:05.619 --> 00:50:07.018
Skip...

529
00:50:07.588 --> 00:50:10.216
...what are you gonna do
about those sets? They suck.

530
00:50:10.858 --> 00:50:12.587
We ain't doing nothing.

531
00:50:14.228 --> 00:50:15.820
The boys been talking?

532
00:50:16.530 --> 00:50:18.157
About how I lost it?

533
00:50:19.633 --> 00:50:23.262
Billy Tyne's lost it? Gets a little
slow. they'll draw and quarter you.

534
00:50:24.405 --> 00:50:26.532
I just didn't think
you'd go along with it.

535
00:50:27.041 --> 00:50:30.841
I come here because I need the money.
I'm trying for a new start.

536
00:50:31.045 --> 00:50:33.377
Last trip I thought you had
something to offer.

537
00:50:33.580 --> 00:50:35.707
But all in all.
you're just a little punk.

538
00:50:36.784 --> 00:50:40.550
- You promised me a shitload of fish!
- You'll get a shitload of fish.

539
00:50:40.754 --> 00:50:44.155
I've been in bad patches so many times
and came home with so much stock...

540
00:50:44.358 --> 00:50:47.191
...little boys like you had to
pack it on the pier.

541
00:50:47.394 --> 00:50:49.988
I always find the fish! Always!

542
00:50:50.197 --> 00:50:53.189
And I will this time!
So don't fuck with me!

543
00:50:55.402 --> 00:50:56.994
Aye. aye. skip.

544
00:51:12.486 --> 00:51:13.714
Put them closer!

545
00:51:14.321 --> 00:51:18.314
Murph. closer!
Give them a goddamn banquet.

546
00:51:18.525 --> 00:51:20.186
Aye. aye. cap.

547
00:51:20.961 --> 00:51:23.429
You heard him. boys.
Boss ain't happy.

548
00:51:23.630 --> 00:51:25.097
Double-time.

549
00:51:27.134 --> 00:51:28.123
Let's go. Bob.

550
00:51:31.972 --> 00:51:33.098
Sullivan!

551
00:51:33.807 --> 00:51:36.332
I gotta hit you with a fish again
to get you to work?

552
00:51:36.543 --> 00:51:37.908
Lightsticks. now!

553
00:51:38.112 --> 00:51:39.875
Shut up. asshole!

554
00:51:40.080 --> 00:51:42.344
You couldn't bait fish in a barrel!

555
00:51:43.617 --> 00:51:46.586
- Come on.
- See what I got to deal with?

556
00:51:46.787 --> 00:51:48.482
That's a landlubber.
What an idiot!

557
00:51:48.689 --> 00:51:51.715
Come on. Sully.
What are you. a fisherman or a farmer?

558
00:51:51.925 --> 00:51:53.517
Bugs. help him out.

559
00:51:53.727 --> 00:51:56.093
Hurry up. before the captain sees.

560
00:51:56.363 --> 00:51:59.560
Okay. sure. I'll help him out.
What a screwup!

561
00:51:59.767 --> 00:52:02.998
- You're useless. Sully!
- Lay off. Bugs. You never screw up?

562
00:52:03.203 --> 00:52:06.036
You're nothing but a pimple
on the ass of progress.

563
00:52:06.240 --> 00:52:08.265
I've been on a better slab than this.

564
00:52:08.475 --> 00:52:10.102
I've had it with this.

565
00:52:19.286 --> 00:52:21.049
Take it easy.
It was an accident.

566
00:52:26.493 --> 00:52:29.758
You got the easiest job on the boat.
and you manage to screw it up!

567
00:52:29.963 --> 00:52:32.989
Kiss my ass. you little runt.
And you...!

568
00:52:35.469 --> 00:52:36.367
Murph!

569
00:52:40.407 --> 00:52:42.671
Cap. man overboard!

570
00:52:51.585 --> 00:52:53.314
Take the wheel!

571
00:53:09.903 --> 00:53:11.530
Back her down slow.
